java.intro:
A `static` field belongs to the class, not to one object. Every object sees the same one.
A `static` method is called on the class: `Ticket.issued()`.

```java
class Ticket {
    static int next = 1;
    int id;
    Ticket() { id = next++; }
}
```

`id` is different on each ticket. `next` is the shared counter.

